concept zettelkasten {
  name     = "Zettelkasten"
  summary  = "A method of building knowledge as a web of small, self-contained notes that link to each other rather than sit in a fixed hierarchy — the model a wskill follows."
  related  = [atomic_note, permanent_note, fleeting_note, selfcontained, datapresentation]
  body {
    p <<BODY
      Zettelkasten ("slip-box") is a note-taking method: instead of long documents or a rigid
      folder tree, you keep many small notes, each capturing one idea in your own words, and
      connect them with explicit links. Knowledge emerges from the connections — a note's
      value comes as much from what it links to as from what it says. Structure is grown
      bottom-up from the links, not imposed top-down by a hierarchy.
    BODY

    p <<BODY
      A wskill is a Zettelkasten with a type system. Its units — concepts, entities, facts and
      processes — are the slips; each is an atomic, self-contained note with a stable id, and
      the `related` field is the link between them. The templates then read that web of notes
      and project it into a book or a skill, so the same slip-box becomes several outputs.
    BODY
  }
}
